{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`. A domain is cloneable and safe to share between\nexecutions. The following chapters introduce its members one capability at a\ntime.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    type Error: Send;\n    type NodeData: Clone + Eq + Hash + Send + Sync;\n    type NodeContent: NodeContents;\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n\n    fn cache(&self) -> &ValidationCache<Self>;\n    fn node_path(&self, node: &NodeId<Self>) -> NodePath;\n    fn node_content(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n    fn outgoing_edges(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        label: Self::EdgeLabel,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<NodeId<Self>>, Self::Error>;\n    fn load_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<Record<Self::NodeData, Self::EdgeLabel>>, Self::Error>> + Send;\n    fn store_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &NodeId<Self>,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<Self::NodeData, Self::EdgeLabel>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send;\n\n    fn project_sources(&self) -> Option<SourceProject<Self>> { ... }\n    fn source_node(\n        &self,\n        item: &OutlineData,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeData, SourceError> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.domain`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n- Every application domain implements `Domain`.\n- A domain is `Clone + Send + Sync` and safe to share between executions.\n- The associated types carry their stated bounds:\n  - `Error: Send`\n  - `NodeData: Clone + Eq + Hash + Send + Sync`\n  - `NodeContent: NodeContents`\n  - `EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync`\n- The required members behave as the signatures say: `cache`, `node_path`, `node_content`, `outgoing_edges`, `load_evidence` and `store_evidence`. The two evidence futures must be `Send`.\n- The defaulted members `project_sources` and `source_node` exist with default behavior.\n- The chapters that introduce each member specify its detailed behavior, so those chapters' tests cover it.\n\n**Test mapping**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` is the main test.\n  - It implements `Domain` for a fixture with opaque `Identity` and `Label` types. The fixture's error type is `Send` but not `Sync`, `Debug` or `Clone`.\n  - The generic `check_bounds` function compiles against the declared bounds. It checks that the domain is `Clone + Send + Sync`, that `NodeData` and `EdgeLabel` meet their bounds, that `Error` is `Send`, and that `NodeContent` is `NodeContents + Send + Sync`. It also checks that both evidence futures are `Send`, so loosening or tightening a bound breaks compilation.\n  - The test asserts the defaults: `project_sources()` is `None`, and `source_node` returns `SourceError::Invalid`.\n  - It asserts `node_content` output through `format` and `fingerprint`, and `node_path` segments, including that different nodes give different paths.\n  - It asserts `outgoing_edges` for repeated and ordered successors, an empty result, and an error that survives as a `Send`-only value.\n  - It asserts that `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` run and return the expected results.\n- Sharing between executions is covered by several tests:\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads]`\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls]`\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces]`\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records]`\n- Other tests use `Domain` implementations end to end for contents, edges, and evidence storage and loading:\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]`\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/tests.rs#fn[deterministic_validation_uses_required_storage_without_an_agent]`\n  - `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]`\n  - `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` covers a real application domain's content formatting.\n\n**Minor observation, not a gap**\n- `check_bounds` does not assert `Hash` on `NodeData`. The `Identity` fixture derives `Hash`, and `ValidationCache` interning relies on it, so dropping the bound would most likely break the library or cache code. I did not confirm this in the cache implementation.\n- The detailed behavior of each member is owned by its introducing chapter's requirements, which are assessed separately.",
  "references": "def95cddcfd729d8ab2a7869cd3b7c1d236dc0d2686efb64ec30c6a98a2e742a",
